      "side": 0,
      "message": "I understand the need for this change, but I feel it might be quite invasive.\n\nWhen this change is merged, all plugins will be immediately impacted and will need to migrate to Bzlmod. Given the compatibility option I mentioned earlier, would it be possible to consider a more gradual approach for plugin authors?\n\nPerhaps we could temporarily support both modes:\n\n* New Bzlmod build\n* The old external_plugin_deps.bzl\n\nThis would allow for an easier transition and enable users to upgrade from Bazel 7.x to 8.x without forcing an immediate migration.\n\nOf course, this wouldn\u0027t be viable in the long term, especially with future versions like Bazel 9.x (which hasn’t been released yet). But I think this approach would offer more flexibility for plugin authors during the transition period.\n\nWhat do you think?",
      "revId": "ff62ab90fe09386ac5db9dd1d0b5d4fcffd975fb",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
